[{:seon.task/name "templates-are-held-task-data"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the templates a task can be started from are maps (`seon.template/templates`) merged onto what was asked (`seon.template/from`), the first step; their text is still strings in `seon.template/instructions`, keyed by `:seon.task/kind`; `seon.template/request` is the :whole map, `seon.template/design-build` :work's into its design-build task and `seon.template/with-merge` :merge's into its merge, and `seon.template/stages` copies :design's and :implement's into its stages; `seon.task/accumulate` hard-codes which members flow, and proofs accumulate along :needs (docs/tasks.md#a-request-is-one-transaction says this is unsettled). Owner, 2026-10-22 (DECISIONS): templates are held tasks in resources/seon/tasks, loaded by `my.root/load-tasks!`; ``:seon.task/owned`` on each member's schema says what carries; proofs are owned, not carried; design writing implement's proofs is seon.task/design-writes-the-implement-steps-proofs; `:seon.task/kind` goes, and the attributes present decide (a merge carries :seon.task/target). Deletes: `seon.template/instructions`, the join in `seon.task/accumulate`, :seon.task/kind."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.task/design-writes-the-implement-steps-proofs"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.template-test/a-template-is-a-held-task seon.task-test/owned-members-carry-by-schema-property seon.task-test/proofs-never-accumulate}}]
